## 8.5 Tolerance evaluation

Use explicit feature-level acceptance criteria.

For symmetric scalar tolerances:

Error = Measured Value - Target Value

Pass if:

|Error| ≤ Tolerance.

For asymmetric tolerances, use explicit minimum and maximum permitted values.

A measurement with missing or invalid data must never return PASS.

A missing tolerance must not be silently assumed.

Preserve the tolerance definition used during the original evaluation.

