## 9.2 Calculated clearance

When compatible mating dimensions exist, calculate signed diametral clearance using the explicitly defined convention:

Clearance = Internal Feature Diameter - Mating External Diameter.

Positive values indicate dimensional clearance.

Negative values indicate interference.

Do not automatically translate positive clearance into confirmed assembly success.

Consider measurement uncertainty and geometric limitations.

If mating measurements are unavailable, do not fabricate clearance values.

## 9.3 Assembly outcome

Provide a clear distinction between:

- Predicted fit based on dimensional calculations.
- Measured geometric compatibility.
- Actual physical assembly test.

Actual physical verification must not be inferred from a software calculation.

